== no_x
error[Z0401]: `errorbars` places its intervals along `x`, but the plot maps no variable to `x`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:17
  |
3 | m.plot(y: mean).errorbars(low: lower, high: upper)
  |                 ^^^^^^^^^ needs `x`
  |
  = help: map it where the plot starts, as in `plot(x: arm, y: mean).errorbars(low: lower, high: upper)`

== a_low_of_text
error[Z0401]: `errorbars` draws `low` on a linear scale, so `name` must be a Bool, Int or Float variable, but it is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:18
  |
3 | p.errorbars(low: name, high: upper)
  |                  ^^^^ not a numeric variable
  |
  = help: the ends of an interval are numbers; `m.describe()` lists the types of the variables

== a_high_of_dates
error[Z0401]: `errorbars` draws `high` on a linear scale, so `day` must be a Bool, Int or Float variable, but it is a Date
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:31
  |
3 | p.errorbars(low: lower, high: day)
  |                               ^^^ not a numeric variable
  |
  = help: the ends of an interval are numbers; `m.describe()` lists the types of the variables

== a_y_axis_of_categories
error[Z0401]: `errorbars` places its two ends on a linear scale, but the `y` axis of this plot holds the categories of `name`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:25
  |
3 | m.plot(x: arm, y: name).errorbars(low: lower, high: upper)
  |                         ^^^^^^^^^ needs numbers along `y`
  |
  = help: `points` and `lines` are placed on an axis of categories; `errorbars` needs a number along `y`

== a_y_axis_of_dates
error[Z0401]: `errorbars` places its two ends on a linear scale, but the `y` axis of this plot holds the dates of `day`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:24
  |
3 | m.plot(x: arm, y: day).errorbars(low: lower, high: upper)
  |                        ^^^^^^^^^ needs numbers along `y`
  |
  = help: `points`, `lines` and `step` are placed on a scale of dates; `errorbars` needs a number along `y`, and may have dates along the other axis

== a_low_that_is_not_there
error[Z0101]: no variable `lowest` in `m`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:18
  |
3 | p.errorbars(low: lowest, high: upper)
  |                  ^^^^^^ not a variable of m
  |
  = help: did you mean `lower`? If you meant a category level, write it in quotes: `"lower"`

== a_low_in_another_case
error[Z0102]: no variable `Lower` in `m`; names are case-sensitive
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:18
  |
3 | p.errorbars(low: Lower, high: upper)
  |                  ^^^^^ differs only in case from `lower`
  |
  = help: write `lower`

== a_width_below_nothing
error[Z0401]: `width:` of `errorbars` is the width of a cap as a share of the gap between two values of `x`, from 0 to 1, but this is -0.1
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:45
  |
3 | p.errorbars(low: lower, high: upper, width: -0.1)
  |                                             ^^^^ not a share
  |
  = help: write 0 for intervals without caps, or a share such as 0.5 for caps half as wide as the gap; without `width:` a cap is 0.3 of the gap

== a_width_above_one
error[Z0401]: `width:` of `errorbars` is the width of a cap as a share of the gap between two values of `x`, from 0 to 1, but this is 1.5
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:45
  |
3 | p.errorbars(low: lower, high: upper, width: 1.5)
  |                                             ^^^ not a share
  |
  = help: write 0 for intervals without caps, or a share such as 0.5 for caps half as wide as the gap; without `width:` a cap is 0.3 of the gap

