== an_end_below_nothing_on_a_log_axis
error[Z0401]: `lower - 2` has 2 values at or below 0, which have no place on a log scale: rows 1 and 4 of m
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:16
  |
3 | p.scale_y(log).errorbars(low: lower - 2, high: upper)
  |                ^^^^^^^^^ the `y` axis is a log scale
  |
  = help: keep the rows with a value above 0, as in `where(lower - 2 > 0)`; a square-root scale, `sqrt`, holds 0

== intervals_of_a_frame
error[Z0401]: `errorbars` cannot be called on a Frame
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:1
  |
3 | m.errorbars(low: lower, high: upper)
  | ^ this is a Frame
  |
  = help: `errorbars` takes a Plot first; `x.errorbars(...)` is `errorbars(x, ...)`

== a_frame_without_the_variable
error[Z0101]: no variable `arm` in `the frame`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:19
  |
3 | p.errorbars(data: frame(site = ["a"], from = [1], to = [2]), low: from, high: to)
  |   --------- this layer draws `arm`, which the plot maps to `x`
  |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not a variable of the frame
  |
  = help: the variables of `the frame` are: site, from, to
